# Git Workflow Rules

## Branch Strategy

Two permanent branches:

| Branch | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `main` | Production-ready, stable. Receives merges from `develop` only. Never commit directly. |
| `develop` | Integration branch. All feature branches merge here first. |

**Flow:** `feature branch` → PR → `develop` → PR → `main`

## Branch Naming

Branches are named after the **feature**, not the phase. Do not include phase numbers.

```
<type>/<short-feature-description>

feat/rich-text-editor
feat/tag-system
fix/notification-duplicate
chore/upgrade-prisma
refactor/thread-queries
```

| Prefix | Usage |
|--------|-------|
| `feat/` | New feature |
| `fix/` | Bug fix |
| `chore/` | Configuration, tooling, dependency updates |
| `refactor/` | Code improvement without behavior change |
| `docs/` | Documentation-only change |

## Commit Message Format (Conventional Commits)

**All commit messages must be in English.**

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

feat(editor): add TipTap markdown support
fix(auth): redirect to login when session expires
chore(deps): update prisma to 7.x
refactor(queries): extract thread queries to separate file
```

### Type List

| Type | When |
|------|------|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `chore` | Build, config, dependencies |
| `refactor` | Restructuring |
| `style` | Format/style only (no behavior change) |
| `test` | Adding/editing tests |
| `docs` | Documentation |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |

### Scope Examples

`auth`, `threads`, `posts`, `categories`, `users`, `admin`, `db`, `ui`, `api`, `editor`, `tags`, `search`, `notifications`

## PR Rules

### Feature → develop

- PR targets `develop`, never `main`
- Title in commit format: `feat(editor): add TipTap markdown support`
- Include Linear issue ID in description: `Closes DRA-45` (use the real issue key from Linear; see `ROADMAP.md`)
- Before merging:
  - [ ] Build passes (`npm run build`)
  - [ ] No TypeScript errors (`tsc --noEmit`)
  - [ ] Tests pass if any exist

### develop → main

- Open PR from `develop` → `main`
- Title: `release: <brief description of included features>`
- All features must be stable and tested
- Merging triggers Coolify production deploy

## Working with Multiple Agents (Claude Code + Cursor)

To avoid conflicts when two agents work simultaneously:

- **Each agent works on a different branch** — never work on the same branch concurrently
- Always branch off from `develop`, not `main`
- Check branch status with `git status` before starting a new task
- Before committing, stay up to date with `git pull origin develop --rebase`
- If two agents are editing the same file simultaneously → finish one, merge it to develop, then start the other

## Forbidden Actions

- Direct push to `main` or `develop`
- `git push --force` (to main or develop)
- Branching off from `main` for features (always use `develop` as base)
- `.env` file in a commit
- Commit containing `console.log` (remove development logs before committing)
- Commit containing `TODO:` comments (open a Linear issue instead)
